# THE TOOLCHAIN THIS REPOSITORY IS BUILT WITH. ONE FILE, AND IT IS THE ONLY ONE
# THAT PINS A VERSION.
#
# `mise install` reads this directly, so a clean clone installs the exact
# versions rather than guessing from a floating major. `.github/workflows/ci.yml`
# installs from this same file through `jdx/mise-action` and re-declares NONE of
# the four strings itself. `bin/check-toolchain.sh` fails the build if a literal
# is ever copied back beside the manifest — that is a second source of truth with
# nothing reconciling it against the first, and it is the arrangement this
# repository spent its first month policing before the copies were deleted on
# 2026-08-26.
#
# The names are mise's, which are also asdf's for three of the four. Where the
# workflow WOULD spell each one, were a copy ever reintroduced, is the closed
# table in `ci_declared` in that gate:
#
#     erlang       ->  erlef/setup-beam    otp-version
#     rebar        ->  erlef/setup-beam    rebar3-version
#     node         ->  actions/setup-node  node-version
#     tree-sitter  ->  npm                 tree-sitter-cli@<version>
#
# The tree-sitter CLI is one binary under two names: mise builds it from the
# `tree-sitter/tree-sitter` release, CI takes the npm package `tree-sitter-cli`,
# and both publish the same version number.
#
# ONE REQUIRED TOOL HAS NO LINE BELOW, AND IS NAMED HERE ANYWAY: python3.
#
# `compiler/bin/check-switch-diagnostics.sh` shells to
# `handoff/audition-switch/build-packet.py --check`, which asks whether the
# committed `PACKET.md` is what `LANGUAGE.md` sections 2, 3 and 5 would produce
# today. `handoff/audition-switch/run.sh` and `stage.sh` shell to it as well.
# That makes python3 a hard dependency of a gate that runs in `verify.sh` and in
# CI, and of the audition harness.
#
# Until 2026-08-28 it was named in no manifest, no workflow step, no gate and no
# README, while the first line of this file called it the only record of what the
# repository is built with. Every build was green throughout, because the pinned
# runner image and the Xcode command line tools each happen to ship a python3. An
# accident that holds on both machines a project is developed on is precisely the
# one that breaks on somebody else's.
#
# IT IS DELIBERATELY NOT PINNED, and the asymmetry with the four below is the
# decision rather than an oversight. Those are pinned because each has a second
# declaration to drift from and because the artifacts they produce depend on
# their version. Neither holds here: both scripts import only `io`, `os`, `re`
# and `sys`, and what they write is sections of `LANGUAGE.md` copied verbatim, so
# every python3 emits the same bytes. A version line would assert a requirement
# nobody has measured — and this repository has already been caught believing a
# declared version string that was not what arrived.
#
# `bin/check-toolchain.sh --env` checks that it is PRESENT, and says so before
# anything compiles. A missing python3 is not something `mise install` can fix.

erlang 28.5
rebar 3.27.0
node 24.19.0
tree-sitter 0.25.10
